WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.588
DNA polymerase can catch its own typos.

00:00:03.215 --> 00:00:04.155
Watch it copy.

00:00:05.003 --> 00:00:06.199
Oops, a wrong base.

00:00:06.919 --> 00:00:08.022
Polymerase backs up.

00:00:08.312 --> 00:00:09.693
It snips the wrong base off the

00:00:09.763 --> 00:00:10.622
3-prime end.

00:00:10.912 --> 00:00:12.120
Then it adds the right one.

00:00:12.306 --> 00:00:14.070
Like hitting backspace while you type.

00:00:14.523 --> 00:00:15.928
This is called proofreading.

00:00:16.462 --> 00:00:18.621
Proofreading fixes a wrong base right away,

00:00:18.772 --> 00:00:20.235
while DNA is being copied.

00:00:20.955 --> 00:00:22.418
What about mistakes found later?

00:00:23.044 --> 00:00:23.648
Swipe.
